A||||5||Homicidal||How do I remove the wheel lock on my front tires?||||1||
Z||000000||Homicidal||06-20-2000||03:43 AM||||My two front tires have one wheel lock each in place of the lug nuts.  How do I remove this sucker??||||reg||1
Z||000001||RossT||06-20-2000||03:59 AM||||1. <A HREF="http://home.xnet.com/~nife/articles/tt-lugpanic.html" TARGET=_blank>http://home.xnet.com/~nife/articles/tt-lugpanic.html</A> <P>2. <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/004288.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/004288.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||triker||06-20-2000||11:42 AM||||Find someone with an arc welder to tack a 1/2 nut on the locking nut, then use a 3/4 in socket to remove it.||||reg||1
Z||000003||lennyb4||06-20-2000||11:48 AM||||Most shops will remove it with a nut cracker for about $10US.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Big O||06-21-2000||07:33 AM||||At my shop we have a set of sockets specifically for removing lock nuts.  Yes you hammer them on and the nut is usually damaged to some extent, but it comes of pretty easily.  We don't charge anything for the service.||||reg||1
Z||000005||ThatRickGuy||06-21-2000||04:57 PM||||gess, guess I'm a strange one... I just used the adaptor that was in the counsle glove box...||||reg||1
